<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xie Xuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">343–388</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xie Xuan was a Chinese general of the Eastern Jin dynasty and nephew of the statesman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xie-an">Xie An</a>. In 377 he raised the Beifu, or 'Northern Headquarters', army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jingkou">Jingkou</a> from refugees from the north, which became the dynasty's best fighting force. He led the vanguard that routed the much larger Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river">Battle of Fei River</a> in 383 and then recovered territory south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xie-xuan.jpg" alt="Xie Xuan" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%99%89%E5%BA%B7%E6%A8%82%E7%8D%BB%E6%AD%A6%E5%85%AC%E8%AC%9D%E7%8E%84.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
